there's more detail in that little box than in any of those games.

00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:45.680
Like that, I mean, I'm not saying that this is beautiful graphics, but it's more than just basically a wireframe of a hallway.

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:58.480
At least there's color, there's texture, there's some semblance of it being a place instead of a, uh, a Windows 95's, uh, like, screen saver.

00:07:58.480 --> 00:08:07.240
Right. Uh, and you know, for a game that has a lot of, uh, details to it of just even learning how to play this kind of game,

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:12.620
I mean, you think about, you know, not everybody was playing every single NES game that released in North America.

